{
  "version": 1,
  "title": "Choose the sanitizer for the failure",
  "hook": "What do ASan, UBSan and TSan instrument, and what do they cost?",
  "topic": "compilers/opt/sanitizers-asan-ubsan-tsan",
  "tags": [
    "compilers",
    "asan",
    "ubsan",
    "tsan"
  ],
  "level": "intermediate",
  "series": "compilers-optimization-debugging",
  "series_index": 3,
  "scenes": [
    {
      "duration_ms": 11000,
      "caption": "ASan checks memory accesses against runtime tracking.",
      "narration": "A heap crash appears far from its cause. Build with symbols and AddressSanitizer; it instruments accesses and tracks memory state to catch many bounds and lifetime errors.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "heading",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "Start with memory",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 5,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 12,
          "at": 0,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "inspect",
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sh",
          "text": "clang -O1 -g \\\n  -fno-omit-frame-pointer \\\n  -fsanitize=address \\\n  app.c -o app-asan",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 22,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 34,
          "at": 600,
          "enter": "slide-up"
        },
        {
          "id": "checks",
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "Reports may include allocation and free stacks",
            "Typical documented slowdown: about 2×"
          ],
          "x": 8,
          "y": 64,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 24,
          "color": "green",
          "at": 3400,
          "enter": "slide-up"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "duration_ms": 10500,
      "caption": "UBSan targets selected undefined operations, not all possible bugs.",
      "narration": "Add undefined behavior checks for cases such as signed overflow and misalignment. Cost depends on checks and workload; this does not prove your program is defined.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "heading",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "Add UB checks",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 5,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 12,
          "at": 0,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "inspect",
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sh",
          "text": "clang -O1 -g \\\n  -fsanitize=address,undefined \\\n  app.c -o app-check\n./app-check",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 22,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 34,
          "at": 600,
          "enter": "slide-up"
        },
        {
          "id": "checks",
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "ASan and UBSan can be combined",
            "Read the first actionable report"
          ],
          "x": 8,
          "y": 64,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 24,
          "color": "green",
          "at": 3400,
          "enter": "slide-up"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "duration_ms": 10000,
      "caption": "TSan tracks memory accesses and synchronization to detect races.",
      "narration": "An intermittent counter mismatch needs a separate ThreadSanitizer build. It tracks conflicting accesses and synchronization; the documented typical runtime overhead is five to fifteen times.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "heading",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "Build for races",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 5,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 12,
          "at": 0,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "inspect",
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sh",
          "text": "clang -O1 -g -pthread \\\n  -fsanitize=thread \\\n  race.c -o race-tsan\n./race-tsan",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 22,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 34,
          "at": 600,
          "enter": "slide-up"
        },
        {
          "id": "checks",
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "Do not combine TSan with ASan",
            "Typical TSan memory overhead: 5–10×"
          ],
          "x": 8,
          "y": 64,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 24,
          "color": "green",
          "at": 3400,
          "enter": "slide-up"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "duration_ms": 10000,
      "caption": "Sanitizers diagnose executed paths; workload coverage still matters.",
      "narration": "Run the failing workload, inspect the reported stacks, and fix ownership or synchronization. Repeat with the same input, then add varied scheduling and boundary cases.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "heading",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "Reproduce, then repair",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 5,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 12,
          "at": 0,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "node0",
          "type": "box",
          "text": "Failing input → sanitizer report",
          "x": 15,
